xnu 0132: power the touch part the way the vendor does, and speak Goodix SPI

Three fixes, all visible in one boot:

- The reset line is active high in the live tree (flags 0), so the old code
  held the part in reset while calling it a release. Assert it while AVDD
  settles, then release it low, 150 ms before the first transfer.
- IOVDD (pm8350c_l2) is an RPMh vote and used to be cast after the part was
  already out of reset. Vote it first: voltage 1800 mV at +0x0 (the vendor
  driver sends millivolts), enable at +0x4 and PMIC5 LDO mode 7 (HPM, not the
  DT's RPMH mode 4) at +0x8, three commands in one TCS. CMD_MSGID_LEN is 8 in
  both the vendor and mainline rpmh-rsc, not 3.
- The transfer used to guess the framing. The Goodix SPI protocol is a 0xF1
  read (0xF0 write) byte, the address as 32-bit big endian and three dummy
  bytes, all inside one CS frame (drivers/hid/hid-goodix-spi.c). The probe now
  writes eight 0xAA bytes to 0x10000 and reads them back, which proves power,
  reset and framing at once, then reads the classic id at 0x8140.

